WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:05.240
This is YourKhata. All of your business's records, in one place.

2
00:00:05.741 --> 00:00:10.940
This video takes six everyday problems, and solves each one, a step at a time.

3
00:00:11.933 --> 00:00:19.380
The first problem. You open a new app and it is full of buttons, half of which are not for your work.

4
00:00:19.882 --> 00:00:26.401
Say you are starting today, and you want only the things your own work needs.

5
00:00:27.401 --> 00:00:34.044
The answer is simple. Signing up takes only a mobile number. There is no password.

6
00:00:34.546 --> 00:00:39.374
Press Send code, and type the four-digit code that arrives by SMS.

7
00:00:39.874 --> 00:00:43.307
Now fill in the business name, your own name and your state.

8
00:00:45.079 --> 00:00:50.727
Then choose what you need. You can pick one, or more than one.

9
00:00:51.226 --> 00:00:56.625
We chose Shop, so it asks only what kind of shop. Now Continue.

10
00:00:57.125 --> 00:01:03.676
GST and the address can wait. The last screen says back what you chose.

11
00:01:05.358 --> 00:01:12.707
The benefit: the menu shows only what you chose. Anything else can be added later, whenever you want.

12
00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:20.117
The second problem: money given on credit. The notebook cannot be found, and memory does not hold.

13
00:01:20.618 --> 00:01:25.947
A customer says, but I already paid you. What will you show them?

14
00:01:26.967 --> 00:01:33.853
The answer: an account for every customer. Open Customers, and there is who owes how much.

15
00:01:34.353 --> 00:01:40.223
Open the account of Ramesh Traders. Every entry is written down with its date.

16
00:01:40.723 --> 00:01:46.879
Today he paid five hundred rupees. Press You got, type the amount, and save.

17
00:01:47.381 --> 00:01:53.809
The balance changed at once. The benefit: no arguments about the account, and money collected on time.

18
00:01:54.800 --> 00:02:01.927
The third problem: making a bill. By hand it takes time, and the tax gets added wrong.

19
00:02:02.427 --> 00:02:06.403
The counter is busy, and the customer wants a proper bill right now.

20
00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.435
The answer: open a new bill and choose the customer.

21
00:02:11.298 --> 00:02:13.760
Add the item, and type the quantity.

22
00:02:14.608 --> 00:02:21.163
GST was added by itself. CGST and SGST are shown separately.

23
00:02:21.664 --> 00:02:27.574
Press Issue. The bill is ready, to print or to send on WhatsApp.

24
00:02:28.074 --> 00:02:33.893
The benefit: a correct bill in moments, and what was sold has come off the stock by itself.

25
00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:42.131
The fourth problem. You learn that something has run out only when a customer leaves empty-handed.

26
00:02:42.631 --> 00:02:47.737
And at the end of the month, adding up sales and tax is a headache of its own.

27
00:02:48.733 --> 00:02:54.657
The answer: Items holds all your stock. Press Low, and it shows what is running short.

28
00:02:55.157 --> 00:03:01.480
Reports has the day book, what is owed, sales and the GST summary, all ready.

29
00:03:02.659 --> 00:03:08.109
The benefit: you reorder in time, and never sit down separately to add things up.

30
00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:14.160
The fifth problem belongs to any work where members pay a fee every month.

31
00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:21.271
Who has paid, who has not, and which seat is free? You keep turning the pages of a register.

32
00:03:22.266 --> 00:03:29.401
The answer: Library. This business runs only Library. The first screen is today at a glance.

33
00:03:29.902 --> 00:03:35.681
How much in fees is unpaid, how many seats are taken in each shift, and who has to pay.

34
00:03:36.183 --> 00:03:40.786
Students lists every member's plan, seat and fee date.

35
00:03:41.285 --> 00:03:46.348
A new admission. Type the name, then choose the plan, the shift and the seat.

36
00:03:49.469 --> 00:03:54.897
Seats shows which seat is free, and Attendance the daily register.

37
00:03:55.399 --> 00:04:00.477
The benefit: fees remembered without turning a page, and every seat accounted for.

38
00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:07.418
The sixth problem: daily instalments. Whom do you collect from today, and who has already paid?

39
00:04:07.918 --> 00:04:13.133
The collector has already left, and all you have is an old diary.

40
00:04:14.132 --> 00:04:19.732
The answer: Lending. Today is the whole list for the day, with names and amounts.

41
00:04:20.233 --> 00:04:25.973
Press Collect, choose how it was paid, and save. The instalment is recorded.

42
00:04:26.474 --> 00:04:32.522
Loans holds the full schedule of every loan: how many instalments are in, and how many remain.

43
00:04:33.023 --> 00:04:38.054
The benefit: no instalment is missed, and nothing has to be tallied in the evening.

44
00:04:39.065 --> 00:04:45.268
All of this runs under one login. Moving from one business to another is a single tap.

45
00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:53.311
Need something later? Add it from the business menu. If you stop needing it, turn it off.

46
00:04:53.812 --> 00:04:58.213
In Team, add your staff, and decide who can see what.

47
00:04:58.737 --> 00:05:01.277
And the whole app runs in Hindi too.

48
00:05:04.265 --> 00:05:09.640
Start free at yourkhata.com. All you need is a mobile number.

49
00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:15.309
Choose only what you need. And keep your accounts clear from today.
